        "original_id": "07725910-37e9-5113-845f-5d5425f4e9c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maulana Karenga, Hakim Jamal, Malcolm X, Michael X, Allen Donaldson\n- Organizations: US\n- Movements: Black Power movement, black nationalism, social change\n\nFacts:\n- Hakim Abdullah Jamal was the name adopted by African-American activist Allen Donaldson, who was born on March 28, 1931.\n- Maulana Karenga was a major figure in the Black Power movement during the 1960s and 1970s.\n- Maulana Karenga and Hakim Jamal co-founded US, an organization focused on black nationalism and social change.\n- Hakim Jamal was a cousin of Malcolm X and later became an associate of Michael X.\n- Hakim Jamal died on May 1, 1973.",
